# ── Pre-commit gate ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Mirrors the CI checks that need no services, so a failing commit can never
# reach origin. The test suites are not here: run `npm test` (unit, no services)
# and, for a change that touches persistence, `npm run test:int -w apps/api`
# (needs PostgreSQL) before pushing.
#
# `test:catalogue` is the one test file that runs here: it catches drift between
# thrown error codes and their translated messages, which lint and typecheck
# cannot see.
#
# Bypass (only for true emergencies, and fix in the next commit):
#   git commit --no-verify
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

set -e
npm run lint
npm run typecheck
npm run data:lint
npm run test:catalogue
